; resources.eval — the aptitude/practice pools, measured (docs/health-and-healing.md).
;
; Run:  Dungeon.exe -eval tools\EvalScripts\resources.eval
;
; THIS IS A MEASUREMENT, NOT A PASS/FAIL. It prints three tables and the reader
; compares them across a knob change. What it is looking for:
;
;   1. THE ORDERING the model asks for — stamina/sec > mana/sec > health/sec at
;      equal investment. That is a property of the AUTHORED knobs and not of the
;      arithmetic, so RollTest cannot check it and this is where it lives.
;   2. HEALTH REGENERATES AT ALL, which it never did before this system.
;   3. The practices TRAIN off throughput, and — the rule the whole model exists
;      to protect — creep NO stat while doing it.

logecho on
reset

timescale 0
lockstep on
seed 7

; An empty room, so nothing wanders in and turns a regen measurement into a
; combat one. The party is the instrument here.
arena open 9 9

echo === 1. the pools at rest, fresh party ===
party
regen
char 0
char 3

; NOTE the two `ref` rows `regen` prints beneath the party. Those — not the
; member rows — are where the ordering claim is read: the four members differ in
; every stat on purpose, so Brand's mana crawling behind his health is his BUILD
; and not a broken knob.

; Hurt everyone and drain the casters, then let it all come back untouched.
; `effect` puts a real DoT on them rather than a harness fiat, so the damage
; goes through the one pipeline like anything else.
echo === 2. wounded, then sixty idle seconds ===
effect bleed 0 6 4
effect bleed 1 6 4
effect bleed 2 6 4
effect bleed 3 6 4
step 6
echo --- after the bleed ---
party
step 60
echo --- after 60s idle ---
party

echo === 3. what the recovery TRAINED ===
; Constitution should have grown off the points regained, and NOTHING else
; should have moved: no vitality, no other skill. A stat that crept here is the
; runaway walking back in (docs/health-and-healing.md).
char 0
char 3

echo === 4. exertion: the state gate, and conditioning ===
; Marching spends stamina, which holds regen off and trains conditioning. Health
; must NOT come back while that holdoff is up — that is the gate.
effect bleed 0 8 2
step 3
echo --- hurt, about to march ---
party
forward 4
step 1
echo --- mid-march (holdoff up: health and stamina frozen, mana at mana_exert) ---
party
step 30
echo --- 30s standing still afterwards ---
party
char 0

echo === 5. mana: attunement trains, and the school skill is the CONTROL ===
; THE OBSERVATION THAT PROVES TWO THINGS AT ONCE. One cast trains two skills for
; two different reasons: `fire` is what Tilo KNOWS, and it creeps INT/WIL like
; every other skill in the game; `attunement` is what his body PASSED, and it
; must creep nothing at all. Both appear below, and the `creep` lines must name
; the school's stats and only those. Without the school skill in the same run,
; an empty creep list would prove nothing — it would look identical to a run in
; which no skill trained at all.
learn 3 fire
echo --- before casting ---
char 3
cast 3 fire
cast 3 fire
cast 3 fire
step 1
echo --- after three casts (12 mana) ---
char 3
regen

echo === 6. pace: conditioning speeds you up, the party waits anyway ===
; docs/health-and-healing.md "Movement". Conditioning ADDS to a member's
; authored pace, and the party moves at its SLOWEST member's — so the whole
; point is the second row here: training the FASTEST member changes the party
; number by NOTHING. Either everyone trains, or everyone crawls.
;
; Authored: Brand 0.95, Sera 1.20, Maren 1.00, Tilo 0.90 (the anchor).
echo --- as authored ---
regen
echo --- Sera (already fastest) trains hard: no party gain ---
setskill 1 conditioning 30
regen
echo --- Tilo (the anchor) trains instead: the party finally moves ---
setskill 3 conditioning 30
regen

state
